{
  "Cabin.Stage.1.Description": "Now that you've harvested some trees, you can now make some plans. You start with taking some of the inner bark of the trees you've harvested and pounding it flat. It makes primitive but useful paper. A chunk of charcoal from your campfire and a few moments with a blade make a nice point. Now you can draw up some plans for your cabin.[pg]"
  "Cabin.Stage.10.Description": "You walk back to your cabin construction site and resume working. You take out the book and flip pages until you come across instructions on how to install wooden flooring.[pg]"
  "Cabin.Stage.10.Name": "[b: You have finished installing the flooring!][pg]"
  "Cabin.Stage.2.Description": "You have the tools and your finished plans. Now you can finally get this cabin off the ground. The first thing you'll need to build is a foundation and flooring. There's enough field stone around from your clearing here to create some simple piers.[pg]"
  "Cabin.Stage.2.Name": "You estimate that it's going to take around 100 nails and 50 units of wood to build your flooring. Do you wish to start now?[pg]"
  "Cabin.Stage.3.Description": "You take a peek through the manual that came with the toolbox and compare its cabin plans with your own before you start.[pg]"
  "Cabin.Stage.3.Name": "[b: You have finished building the foundation!]\nYou can now work on constructing the framing and walls.[pg]"
  "Cabin.Stage.4.Description": "Now that you have a solid foundation in place, it's time to raise the walls and the roof. This is going to take a lot of nails, probably as much as the toolbox can carry. You'll also need quite a bit of wood, around 75 units of it if your math is right.[pg]"
  "Cabin.Stage.4.Name": "Raise walls and the roof? (Cost: 200 Nails and 75 Wood)[pg]"
  "Cabin.Stage.5.Description": "You spend a few minutes consulting your plans, the carpentry manual, and your own memories. The structures in Ingnam are pretty simple. No weird curves or anything. So the basic framing instructions in the book should suffice. You get to work measuring out boards, sawing them to the right length, and nailing them in the proper proportions. You take care in framing out the windows and the door and checking your geometry.[pg]"
  "Cabin.Stage.6.Description": "As soon as dawn hits and you've eaten, you head right back to work. Starting with the roof, you nail stretchers across your rafters. These provide the nailing surface for your primitive roof. You carefully balance yourself on the structure to nail boards one by one across the stretchers to seal up your roof. Then you do the same for the walls. It's definitely primitive, but it'll work for now.[pg]"
  "Cabin.Stage.6.Name": "[b: You have finished constructing the walls and roof!][pg]"
  "Cabin.Stage.7.Name": "You can continue working on your cabin. Do you start work on installing door and window for your cabin? (Cost: 100 nails and 50 wood.)\n"
  "Cabin.Stage.8.Description": "You walk back to your cabin construction site and resume working. You take out the book and flip pages until you come across instructions on how to construct a door.[pg]"
  "Cabin.Stage.8.Name": "[b: You have finished installing the door and window!][pg]"
  "Cabin.Stage.9.Name": "You can continue working on your cabin. Do you start work on installing flooring for your cabin? (Cost: 200 nails and 50 wood.)[pg]"
  "Cabin.Stage.Eight.Description": "You nail stretchers and boards across the rafters."
  "Cabin.Stage.Eight.Name": "Build the Roof"
  "Cabin.Stage.Five.Description": "You draw up simple plans and mark out the footprint."
  "Cabin.Stage.Five.Name": "Draw Plans"
  "Cabin.Stage.Four.Description": "You check your tools and begin preparing beams."
  "Cabin.Stage.Four.Name": "Prepare Tools"
  "Cabin.Stage.Nine.Description": "You fit a door and shutters to the cabin."
  "Cabin.Stage.Nine.Name": "Doors and Shutters"
  "Cabin.Stage.One.Description": "You wistfully think back to your old town and decide to build a cabin of your own."
  "Cabin.Stage.One.Name": "A Home of Your Own"
  "Cabin.Stage.Seven.Description": "You nail boards across the frame to form the walls."
  "Cabin.Stage.Seven.Name": "Build the Walls"
  "Cabin.Stage.Six.Description": "You raise the frame of the cabin."
  "Cabin.Stage.Six.Name": "Raise the Frame"
  "Cabin.Stage.Ten.Description": "You put down the hammer and admire your finished cabin."
  "Cabin.Stage.Ten.Name": "Finish the Cabin"
  "Cabin.Stage.Three.Description": "You decide to build the cabin from wood."
  "Cabin.Stage.Three.Name": "Choose Materials"
  "Cabin.Stage.Two.Description": "You clear a small hill near the portal and level the ground."
  "Cabin.Stage.Two.Name": "Clear the Site"
}
